    "description": "When the Legacy Payment API times out after committing a refund, the payment worker retries without an idempotency key, causing a duplicate refund to be processed.",
    "rationale": "This experiment tests whether the system violates the network-level idempotency invariant by triggering the payment service's documented 'duplicate charge on retry (always, no dedup)' failure mode. The timeout intervention creates the ambiguous state that leads to retry, while the payment service contract guarantees duplicates on retry without idempotency keys.",
    "expectedInvariant": "r04-network-idempotency",
    "interventions": ["timeout", "missing_idempotency_key"],
    "confidence": 0.9
  }
]

